93	7	• Text-to-Speech Resources \nWritten materials can be converted into audio for students with visual impairments or \nreading difficulties. \n• Multilingual Audio and Video \nEducational content can be translated and narrated in multiple languages, supporting \nmultilingual learners and students with limited proficiency in the instructional language. \n• Captioning and Subtitles \nAutomatic captions help students with hearing impairments and improve comprehension \nfor all learners. \n• Narrated Educational Videos \nAI can create narrated presentations and videos that support auditory learners and students \nwho benefit from multimodal instruction. \n15. An educator generates an image for a lesson using an AI tool and uses it directly without \nreview. What five things should they have checked first? \nBefore using an AI-generated image in teaching materials, an educator should check: \n• Accuracy – Verify that all facts, labels, and visual representations are correct. \n• Bias and Representation  – En	8	15	[0.0010647639,0.0021990205,-0.049844395,-0.057865083,0.037528325,-0.0030309637,0.024719417,0.018309722,0.029403394,0.0115303015,0.07264065,-0.038135823,0.023759043,0.091461584,-0.03157156,-0.0188701,-0.0011040271,0.053065896,-0.01878031,-0.07417671,0.11840555,0.04075808,0.088727206,-0.027299397,0.023541661,0.0567257,-0.0068607884,-0.0852665,0.031136539,-0.06930489,-0.02671092,-0.068064466,0.05745551,0.031246748,-0.045886327,0.08442595,0.005903448,0.033077016,0.02461282,-0.03468261,-0.07550694,0.017610177,-0.00056904485,-0.07120892,0.09906389,-0.0077187205,-0.09455501,-0.08024657,0.018636664,0.040034376,-0.09505382,-0.06461048,0.003135008,-0.054712087,-0.090584174,0.05596465,0.03621815,-0.0027826284,0.03748263,0.0018416897,-0.02874025,-0.037649274,0.033148486,0.04473411,0.03265664,0.022572486,-0.04073163,0.0054036425,0.018237015,-0.014328441,-0.08347076,0.045106664,0.08930946,0.07907307,-0.024071338,0.01560945,0.006116732,-0.084201165,0.038319953,-0.06695607,-