95	7	Part 2: \n1. Design a complete chain-of-thought prompt, explain why CoT improves performance, \nand write the model step-by-step solution. \nComplete Chain-of-Thought Prompt: \n• You are a Year 9 mathematics teacher. Solve the following word problem step by step in a \nclear way that students can follow. Show each calculation, explain what each percentage \nmeans, and give the final answer clearly. \n• Problem: A class of 40 students took two exams. 70% passed Exam 1. Of those who passed \nExam 1, 80% also passed Exam 2. Of those who failed Exam 1, 25% passed Exam 2. How \nmany students passed both exams? \n• Why Chain-of-Thought improves performance: \n• Chain-of-thought prompting improves performance because the problem has several steps. \nThe model must first calculate how many students passed Exam 1, then calculate 80% of \nthat group. Without step-by-step reasoning, the model may jump directly to an answe r or \nconfuse “passed Exam 2” with “passed both exams.” CoT makes the reasoning visible,	9	17	[0.07437085,0.10048344,0.04342732,-0.032449927,-0.00822746,-0.0066997637,0.00019568061,0.09505488,0.00045351498,0.06338891,0.040232565,-0.0021915422,0.07215081,0.03561621,0.06715658,0.015621377,-0.06869775,0.0296111,-0.02878565,-0.07960904,-0.030899156,-0.065207325,0.031736806,0.035780814,-0.052586537,0.016828362,-0.018001525,-0.04931532,0.014541813,-0.022051742,-0.021433253,0.012487789,0.029563133,0.048140567,-0.09810633,-0.016900774,-0.01121807,0.032590646,-0.036802612,0.055823933,-0.09071053,-0.00085595425,0.017070672,0.011330444,0.045745246,-0.09245212,-0.044941235,0.016774902,-0.024833165,0.009461692,-0.087609604,-0.04641629,-0.053950306,-0.058136865,-0.0055379733,0.021634487,0.01978784,-0.033822797,-0.042568825,-0.07065559,-0.1332383,-0.008560386,-0.03873494,-0.03230199,0.022198692,0.02302034,0.025516422,0.005071255,0.024499318,0.1288484,-0.0030496505,0.03898335,0.04626151,-0.05239372,0.035881545,0.011471853,-0.027115513,0.06806347,-0.02259288,-0.03845447