79	7	Part 1 : \n1. What are the four core elements of an effective prompt? Briefly describe each one. \nAccording to prompt engineering principles, the four core elements of an effective prompt \nare: \n• Role / Persona – Specifies who the AI should act as, such as an experienced teacher, tutor, \nor curriculum designer. This helps shape the style, depth, and expertise of the response. \n• Task / Instruction – Clearly states what the AI is required to do using specific and action -\noriented instructions. \n• Context / Background  – Provides relevant information such as the students' age, prior \nknowledge, curriculum framework, available resources, and cultural considerations. \n• Output Format – Specifies how the response should be organized, including  \n• structure, word count, tables, bullet points, or any required sections. \n \n2. Explain the difference between zero-shot and few-shot prompting. Give one classroom \nscenario where few-shot is clearly the better choice. \n• Zero-shot prompting asks t	2	1	[0.08180571,0.05070946,0.021320315,-0.023559755,0.010725475,0.0045964243,0.016943868,0.090391695,-0.010429179,0.029176652,0.0026580049,-0.017918661,0.039344996,-0.031448573,0.025669461,-0.0073326775,0.08443997,-0.060263373,-0.011754887,0.008549234,0.02873967,-0.021813735,0.10943249,0.02218491,-0.06778938,0.026544945,0.02180503,-0.07546248,0.004479563,-0.014017939,-0.011067763,-0.033298835,0.1007363,0.09207683,-0.03379192,0.026664592,0.063873515,0.059928756,-0.03699526,0.025649598,-0.10916792,-0.024239603,0.009874128,-0.031696394,0.054856848,-0.007868688,-0.080774225,-0.072569914,-0.053885475,-0.004613342,-0.10048881,-0.035742715,-0.033407003,-0.011776913,-0.07145719,0.064841814,0.038410272,0.013848651,0.041756704,-0.047628324,-0.13923906,-0.0674421,-0.06205124,0.066994876,0.08476711,0.052420817,-0.032199837,-0.030778019,0.072889805,0.019738179,-0.033527862,0.06906759,-0.008743862,0.042310245,0.0035623165,-0.008574134,-0.069476105,0.0033231752,-0.009489862,-0.04