87	7	8. What makes an assessment task 'AI -robust'? Describe three characteristics with \nexamples. \nAn assessment task is considered AI-robust when it is designed in a way that prevents \nstudents from simply relying on AI to complete the work without demonstrating genuine \nunderstanding. \nThree important characteristics of AI-robust assessments are: \n• Personal or Local Context \nTasks require students to use personal experiences or local knowledge that AI cannot easily \nreproduce. \nExample: "Analyze environmental challenges in your own school or local Palestinian \ncommunity." \n• Process-Based Assessment \nStudents must document the development of their ideas over time through drafts, \nreflections, or portfolios. \nExample: A research portfolio containing dated drafts and reflective journals showing how \nideas evolved. \n• Oral Defense or Live Presentation \nStudents explain and justify their work orally, demonstrating authentic understanding. \nExample: Students present their project and answer	5	9	[-0.046146467,0.056055583,-0.07367718,0.009275769,0.042109933,-0.010540155,0.046111263,0.006801264,-0.010145498,0.064435914,-0.046527695,-0.04109017,0.01662712,0.050273243,-0.06880234,0.010640961,0.033495676,-0.03268892,-0.006358729,-0.008594832,0.05089908,0.021255564,0.036210906,-0.0030250214,0.0028408254,0.09525125,-0.032587383,-0.076758675,0.009052166,-0.04324136,0.030331526,-0.0063455445,0.024552811,-0.0012945973,0.025873048,0.113785125,-0.03852135,0.08030562,0.07967634,-0.04636042,-0.100852154,-0.053561803,0.012222928,-0.11771723,0.06235941,-0.10101802,-0.07074982,-0.05715444,-0.0517576,0.053673215,-0.10100184,-0.017285557,0.023102209,-0.06523726,-0.10916396,0.015636988,-0.013652355,0.035088368,-0.0019535222,-0.037288804,-0.035036486,-0.044222467,0.00586198,0.03860338,0.024483021,0.08569617,-0.07723293,0.016240915,0.010247136,0.04263339,-0.017993663,0.09622669,-0.019698815,0.03371028,0.060405053,-0.0018933323,-0.044917226,-0.06624753,0.05781961,-0.007852