88	7	ng how \nideas evolved. \n• Oral Defense or Live Presentation \nStudents explain and justify their work orally, demonstrating authentic understanding. \nExample: Students present their project and answer questions from the instructor during a \nlive defense. \n \n9. What is the difference between acceptable AI assistance and academic dishonesty in \nthe context of student assignments? \nAcceptable AI assistance involves using AI to support learning while openly \nacknowledging its use. Examples include grammar checking, brainstorming ideas, or \ngenerating an initial outline, provided that the student substantially develops the final work \nand discloses AI assistance. \nAcademic dishonesty, on the other hand, occurs when students submit AI-generated work \nas their own without acknowledgment or when AI performs the majority of the intellectual \nwork. This misrepresents the student's actual knowledge and abilities.	5	10	[-0.09000198,0.044496085,-0.00068448845,-0.010576267,-0.012431655,0.017504718,0.041717872,0.0017003359,0.006979182,0.05793783,0.04900751,0.042489696,0.0048123184,0.048997454,-0.026001113,-0.024641361,0.053609956,-0.03619893,-0.038620215,-0.021488478,0.07765021,-0.01600911,0.03901768,-0.035661284,0.03545361,0.041593008,0.02262342,-0.10793455,0.03283177,-0.005360782,-0.018768976,-0.027035404,0.061063927,-0.021168092,-0.054584887,0.021253413,-0.048104748,0.10052537,0.034763526,-0.048733898,-0.070087545,0.0030716073,-0.02418252,-0.07766118,0.00802347,-0.055745345,-0.04309719,-0.016678689,0.0011967742,-0.05448639,-0.079090066,-0.021808725,-0.022579346,-0.017237643,-0.06289891,-0.05257397,0.0033437393,0.08088458,-0.0057931035,0.06382819,0.021759618,0.018119667,0.06740722,-0.012960855,0.032153074,0.073843,-0.06194514,0.018875211,-0.004754663,0.07092562,0.025490148,0.07645797,-0.054664414,0.021477265,0.035102222,-0.0075429026,0.015957028,-0.02067349,0.043446723,-0.062350485,0.009107578,0.07419195,0.01836056,0.03755563,-0.061001007,-0.07370904,-0.030625