89	7	10. Why is AI detection technology alone an insufficient response to AI -assisted academic \ndishonesty? \nAI detection technology alone is insufficient because detection tools are imperfect and \ncontroversial. They can produce false positives , incorrectly identifying genuine student \nwork as AI -generated, and false negatives , failing to detect AI -assisted submissions. \nTherefore, relying solely on detection tools may unfairly penalize students. \nA more effective and sustainable approach is to design AI-robust assessments, incorporate \noral examinations, use process -based assignments, and establish clear institutional policies \nregarding acceptable AI use. \n11. What is a diffusion model? Explain in simple terms how it generates an image from a \ntext prompt. \nA diffusion model is a generative AI model that creates images by learning to reverse a \nprocess of gradually adding noise to images. \nIn simple terms, the process works as follows: \n• During training, the model learns by progre	6	11	[0.02437866,-0.030632148,0.014193792,0.029612256,0.07832727,-0.03345782,-0.0059321546,0.008407666,0.06871006,-0.010974512,0.057664067,0.009263912,0.04455466,0.036038317,-0.07229825,-0.049200997,0.02403366,-0.043752853,-0.086913675,-0.08834582,-0.010257632,-0.010033849,0.008852946,-0.042971395,-0.04811492,0.08262597,0.014701663,-0.17635804,-0.01569112,-0.040127236,0.0534819,-0.027353635,0.02268172,0.07210624,-0.06424562,-0.01819838,-0.06301391,0.01698406,0.066386454,-0.05155858,-0.036624707,-0.05021041,-0.003626199,-0.021020515,0.09259408,-0.051369358,-0.06436726,-0.02272843,-0.0024030346,-0.038467508,-0.07074089,-0.028857287,0.010688766,0.04375852,-0.12861858,-0.03243417,0.066798724,0.0618122,-0.01449644,-0.000117359814,-0.052359257,-0.042115465,-0.03952934,0.0025322854,0.054243222,0.05480946,-0.043134015,0.02376466,0.019727545,0.026435183,0.09822142,0.064534314,-0.0474235,-0.0023425785,0.0423471,-0.027268203,0.012720856,0.024436893,0.09655599,-0.052202575,0.04