90	7	ative AI model that creates images by learning to reverse a \nprocess of gradually adding noise to images. \nIn simple terms, the process works as follows: \n• During training, the model learns by progressively adding noise to real images until they \nbecome pure noise. \n• The model then learns how to reverse this process by removing noise step by step. \n• During image generation, the model starts with random noise and gradually removes the \nnoise while being guided by a text prompt. \n• After many iterations, a coherent image matching the text description is produced. \n12. Name three specific educational applications of AI image generation and explain the \npedagogical benefit of each. \n• Scientific and Technical Diagrams \nAI can generate diagrams such as cell structures, food webs, or circuit diagrams. \nPedagogical benefit: Complex scientific concepts become easier to understand through \nvisualization.	6	12	[-0.008793798,-0.024445174,0.016031316,0.0015800137,0.022483962,-0.049045112,0.019291928,0.0033849615,0.065158345,-0.00059668906,0.036061,-0.03234071,0.07782068,0.042241525,-0.06318279,0.044346996,0.016697856,0.04118021,-0.008971381,-0.0957987,0.029292336,-0.032315083,0.030695,-0.027351832,0.036501408,0.06119179,-0.0026779983,-0.060737714,0.040520895,-0.049660627,0.06572142,-0.046307858,0.06619558,0.0493229,-0.0451048,0.06529388,-0.05363157,0.08020716,0.030093756,0.036635052,-0.032200202,0.002260078,0.018720984,-0.06279203,0.13702552,0.017212646,-0.048094504,-0.09913866,0.04468049,0.0146343745,-0.13134818,-0.07244505,-0.074641526,-0.04066051,-0.015690178,0.055370208,0.040493444,-0.034385633,-0.007818626,0.008172689,0.021020684,-0.027367746,-0.032503325,3.6252538e-06,0.07215724,0.007287788,-0.006889101,0.0210283,0.033385176,-0.048811115,0.013157461,0.07023191,0.033281893,7.591796e-05,0.04102953,0.021711638,-0.032686744,0.032993555,0.04265824,-0.06397244,0.0031995426,-0.028858457,0.029600944,-0.027400404,0.0056249974,0.017030505,0.017936936,-0.028693