100	7	3. Rebuttal to the claim: “Prompt engineering is just a fad.” \nThe claim that prompt engineering is “just a fad” is not accurate. Prompt engineering is \nimportant because the quality of the prompt strongly affects the quality of the AI output. AI \nsystems do not simply “figure it out” in the way a human teacher understa nds classroom \nneeds. They respond based on the clarity, context, and structure provided in the prompt. \nFirst, role prompting demonstrates that prompt design changes the output significantly. For \nexample, asking the AI to “explain photosynthesis” may produce a generic explanation. \nHowever, asking it to “act as a Year 11 biology teacher and explain photosynthesis with a \ncomparison table and common misconceptions” produces a more targeted and pedagogically \nuseful response. The assigned persona affects tone, vocabulary, depth, and instructional \napproach. \nSecond, few-shot prompting shows that examples improve output quality when a specific \nformat is needed. If a tea	11	22	[0.0127803,0.051547237,0.05293731,-0.034863696,0.07261619,-0.030769447,0.026237192,0.088542245,0.001741979,0.005388682,-0.06613823,-0.057742532,0.01293391,-0.032095768,0.012330092,0.013287596,0.011139134,-0.04141868,-0.022211535,-0.014137804,0.022158168,0.037269294,0.10811036,-0.020481043,-0.01942948,0.022445848,0.012520729,-0.061616935,0.0005182489,-0.0019893637,-0.021483852,0.0451011,0.07663289,0.047631856,-0.026748456,0.031928647,0.049095567,0.073138915,0.0108895805,0.011418015,-0.088880755,-0.040668566,0.028675875,-0.011092617,0.018359177,-0.03725778,-0.011200375,-0.10934139,-0.046468247,-0.025149703,-0.1048429,-0.08022563,-0.047770314,-0.049165133,-0.066562586,0.050776448,0.040133435,0.05614426,0.0036652568,-0.01555318,-0.13105036,-0.06907958,-0.035460703,0.0704557,0.12275285,0.027763823,-0.090380736,-0.0032946896,-0.0105381785,0.009750853,0.010509454,0.07136706,-0.004163674,0.04640224,0.022548199,0.023151113,-0.072688185,0.008001782,0.021124568,-0.0288428