103	7	4. Problems with the rubric criterion and corrected version. \n \nOriginal rubric criterion: \n“Excellent (4): The essay is thorough and well-written. Good (3): The essay is mostly good. \nDeveloping (2): The essay is basic. Beginning (1): The essay needs improvement.” \n \nProblems with this rubric: \n• The descriptors are too vague. \n• The levels are not clearly distinguishable. \n• Words like “good,” “basic,” and “needs improvement” do not explain what the student \nactually did. \n• There are no specific criteria such as argument, evidence, organization, or language. \n• The rubric does not tell students how to improve. \n• It is subjective and may lead to inconsistent marking. \n• It does not specify expectations appropriate for a Year 10 essay. \n \nCorrected rubric criterion: Use of Evidence and Explanation in a Year 10 Essay \nExcellent (4): The essay uses several relevant and accurate pieces of evidence. Each piece \nof evidence is clearly explained and directly connected to the main argument.	12	25	[-0.031154202,0.01168779,0.011195686,-0.0040569524,-0.028777873,0.0067936266,-0.043352667,0.009790734,-0.08205712,0.017219441,-0.009089034,0.04748465,-0.01747246,0.046315808,-0.03957722,-0.017607033,0.051727705,-0.010159899,0.027883064,-0.020470904,0.03775045,-0.01746192,0.058796555,-0.016318595,-0.060564786,0.0233114,-0.022792447,-0.018853331,-0.041645996,0.0055084266,-0.024884775,0.0620618,0.07012326,-0.011035716,-0.016051183,0.006055434,0.010926318,0.0777886,0.0077392077,0.12507376,-0.0065708226,-0.058305416,0.002511298,-0.018139465,0.03169996,-0.065979466,0.04260975,-0.0141868545,-0.05467882,0.023539986,-0.10875597,0.039716624,-0.11440619,-0.062038273,-0.035617344,-0.0075218505,-0.010113074,0.009618475,-0.0010555808,-0.10170468,0.029713983,0.017415227,-0.021586912,0.015570207,0.09055626,0.018196609,-0.048313014,-0.019320183,-0.0052149207,0.1474297,-0.0022083712,0.041273393,-0.042399783,0.061399847,-0.0772803,-0.0032869654,-0.0063845553,0.07090002,-0.0