117	7	8. Design a complete multimodal learning resource on “What is AI Hallucination and why \ndoes it matter for students?” \nTopic: AI Hallucination and Why It Matters for Students \nTarget Audience: Secondary school students \nWritten Explanation — Key Points:  AI hallucination happens when an AI system produces \ninformation that sounds confident but is actually false, inaccurate, or unsupported. For \nexample, an AI chatbot may invent a historical date, create a fake citation, or give an incorrect \nexplanation of a scientific concept. \nAI hallucination matters for students because students may trust AI answers without \nchecking them. This can lead to wrong homework answers, weak research, false information \nin essays, and misunderstanding of important topics. AI tools can be helpful for \nbrainstorming, summarizing, and explaining ideas, but they should not be treated as perfect \nauthorities. \nStudents should use AI critically. They should compare AI answers with trusted sources, \ncheck facts,	18	39	[-0.021062266,0.03215695,0.001971138,-0.047862247,0.0818717,-0.024653612,0.036905147,0.05752143,-0.0034357826,0.039504714,-0.027196245,-0.020734228,0.0041766893,0.029227857,0.030123034,0.042644963,0.004457581,0.059244543,-0.07283339,-0.060121503,0.088445924,-0.0027949645,0.035363212,-0.00046472088,-0.015274536,0.1101892,0.021088155,-0.13426837,-0.059053373,-0.07166586,-0.0026914016,0.037633322,-0.03045376,0.030914642,-0.008256411,0.034845494,-0.06291795,0.07458676,0.08948063,-0.020226808,-0.061001033,0.029093793,0.021042477,-0.044711,0.07055259,-0.003782922,-0.094551496,-0.04631053,0.005377448,0.037877526,-0.104862265,-0.033408735,0.006918201,-0.010131886,-0.017285306,0.03234242,0.0006621184,0.041519564,0.0051282113,-0.045493767,0.0025674761,-0.01083278,-0.021636654,-0.060529068,0.023560435,0.03692925,-0.061209496,0.043938268,0.022033572,0.10487486,0.072571345,0.078630894,0.03345074,0.06430071,0.059815094,0.00031877306,-0.030395115,-0.029648522,0.060436,-0.06